"use strict";
const adventure17={slug:"the-tumbleweed-has-right-of-way",title:"The Tumbleweed Has Right of Way",subtitle:"A tumbleweed attacks your car, follows you home, and apparently becomes your responsibility.",scenes:[{title:"Dead Bush Crossing",body:`<p>You are driving home when a tumbleweed the size of a refrigerator rolls into your lane.</p><p>You stop. It stops.</p><p>The driver behind you honks.</p><p>The tumbleweed refuses to be intimidated.</p>`,question:"What do you do?",choices:[["A","Wait for it to cross.","You wait. It waits. You are now in a standoff with a dead bush."],["B","Drive slowly around it.","It changes direction too. You are being defended by vegetation."],["C","Give it a little honk.","Nothing. Apparently tumbleweeds do not respond to criticism."],["D","Let it hit the car.","THUMP. It bounces off your bumper and keeps going. Tucson's cheapest hit-and-run."]],next:1},{title:"It Followed You Home",body:`<p>You escape and make it home.</p><p>You pull into the driveway.</p><p>Something scratches against the garage door.</p><p>It's the tumbleweed.</p><p>You stare at it. It sits there like this was always the plan.</p>`,question:"Apparently you own a tumbleweed now. What do you do?",choices:[["A","Check it for a microchip.","You approach carefully. There is no collar, no tag, and nowhere obvious to insert batteries."],["B","Put out a little water.","Bad idea. A second tumbleweed appears at the end of the driveway. You may have started something."],["C","Post a FOUND TUMBLEWEED notice.","Within minutes someone replies: PLEASE DON'T KEEP IT. SOMEBODY IS PROBABLY WORRIED SICK."],["D","Ignore it.","You close the garage door. Five seconds later: scratch... scratch... scratch. It has learned persistence."]],next:2},{title:"Do Not Feed the Strays",body:`<p>By sunset, three more tumbleweeds have arrived.</p><p>One is against the mailbox. Another is under the car.</p><p>Your original tumbleweed remains proudly beside the garage.</p><p>A neighbor walks past, looks at the group, and says, “Congratulations. You've been chosen.”</p>`,question:"How do you handle your new tumbleweed family?",choices:[["A","Call animal control.","There is a long silence after you explain the species. Then: “Sir, that's a bush.” You look outside. It is waiting by the door. “That's what it wants you to think.”"],["B","Try to return it to the desert.","You load it into the car. Halfway there it blows out again and beats you home."],["C","Name it.","You call it Spike. This is a mistake. Once you name something, legally or emotionally, you're finished."],["D","Put up a NO TUMBLEWEEDS sign.","By morning the sign has blown away and a tumbleweed is sitting where it used to be. Message received."]],next:3},{title:"The Rule Becomes Clear",body:`<p>The next morning, the wind picks up.</p><p>Your tumbleweed rolls out of the driveway toward the street.</p><p>You actually feel a little sad.</p><p>Then it reaches the crosswalk.</p><p>Traffic stops.</p><p>Every car waits while Spike rolls safely across.</p><p>Nobody remembers passing this law.</p>`,question:"How does your adventure end?",final:true,choices:[["A","Wave goodbye.","Spike disappears into the desert with the confidence of something that has never paid registration fees.","The Tumbleweed Has Right of Way","Nobody knows whether it's the law. Nobody wants to be the test case."],["B","Follow it.","You drive two blocks behind Spike until it joins six other tumbleweeds. They appear to be having a meeting.","You Were Only the Foster Home","Spike has found its people. You have found traffic."],["C","Post the whole story online.","Half the comments say to check it for a chip. The other half warn you never to feed a stray tumbleweed.","Tucson Provides Instructions","One commenter simply writes: “Congrats. You've been chosen.”"],["D","Go back inside.","Something scratches against the front door. You open it. A much smaller tumbleweed is sitting there.","It Had a Baby","You sigh and go looking for a water bowl."]] }]};